title: foodShortage
---
<b>The Empty Granary</b>: The storekeeper brings the day's ration ledger. There was too little food for the City. Outside the bakeries, people wait beside cold ovens. On the walls, soldiers ask when their bread will come.
The storekeeper needs {FoodNeed()} provisions for each full day's ration. The remaining merchants demand wartime prices.
-> Purchase three days of emergency grain. ({EmergencyGrainCost()} gold) <<if GetInt("iMoney") >= EmergencyGrainCost()>>
    <<ResolveFoodShortage buy>>
    Grain carts arrive under guard. The storekeeper weighs the sacks himself. The City has enough food for the next three days.
-> Requisition two days of food from noble households. (Noble support −5 points.)
    <<ResolveFoodShortage requisition>>
    Your guards open private granaries and carry the sacks to the public stores. The owners write down everything taken. They will remember the Emperor's need when you next ask for their help.
-> Give the garrison's reserve ration to the people. (One day of food; army morale −5, public morale +2 points.)
    <<ResolveFoodShortage garrison>>
    The reserve wagons turn away from the barracks and towards the bakeries. Civilians receive bread. The soldiers hear where it came from before evening.
-> Endure another day while we seek supplies. (Public morale −3, army morale −2 points.)
    <<ResolveFoodShortage endure>>
    The storekeeper closes the ledger. You send him to look again. Tonight the household eats quietly; beyond its doors, the City grows louder.
===
